2026-10-20T01:08:12.9795290Z -- v4.0.5 — DHW conservation: a cold tank cannot pour hot water
2026-10-20T01:08:12.9795453Z   ok   the booked draw never exceeds the nominal demand
2026-10-20T01:08:12.9795634Z   ok   every step balances: in == out + losses + storage delta
2026-10-20T01:08:12.9795912Z   ok   the inlet floor fabricated nothing — the scaled draw makes it inert
2026-10-20T01:08:12.9796127Z   ok   a cold tank delivers less than the nominal demand, not the same
2026-10-20T01:08:12.9796347Z   ok   and the tank never pins to the inlet pouring imaginary heat
2026-10-20T01:08:12.9796538Z   ok   a tank at the setpoint is debited exactly the nominal draw
2026-10-20T01:08:12.9796753Z   ok   charging cannot pass the tank rating, and the excess is booked
2026-10-20T01:08:12.9796979Z   ok   a tank read above the rating cools at its physical rate, not by fiat
2026-10-20T01:08:12.9797329Z   ok   an inlet above the tank's surroundings manufactures no heat over 24 h
2026-10-20T01:08:12.9797564Z   ok   the tank is not pinned at the inlet: it settles toward its surroundings
2026-10-20T01:08:12.9797769Z   ok   coil split at the default inlet is the historical arithmetic
2026-10-20T01:08:12.9797990Z   ok   a real winter inlet changes the split and keeps the identity exact
